			JEST FOR KIDS 11-0-10
		Riddles and Puns for the 8 to 14 year old

			RIDDLES

What did it take to repair the athlete's injured knee?
    A joint effort=20

Why did the orchestra conductor listen to the baseball game?
    To learn the score

Where do baby fish play?
    On the sea-saw.

What type of music do ghosts prefer?
   Spirituals, of course.

Why did the reporter run to the ice cream shop?
   He was looking for a scoop.

Where do spiders surf?
   On the web.

			SCHOOL WORK

Define : "Sweater": A garment worn by a child when the mother feels =
chilly.

Use "Acquaint" in a sentence: "This is certainly ACQUAINT little place =
you have here."

Headline: Doctor Testifies In Horse Suit

Excuses: "Please excuse Roland from P.E. for a few days. Yesterday he =
fell out of a tree and misplaced his hip."

"I  collect fairy tales," said Tom grimly.

			PUNS & SHORT JOKES

Birds get grouchy in the morning because their bills are over dew.

A pet store had a bird contest with no perches necessary. =20

I dreampt I was a muffler on a car, and then that I was part of the =
wheel. I woke up exhausted and tired.

When I went to buy  milk and ice cream, I got a fair shake.

Those who get to big for their britches will be exposed in the end.

			GROANERS & LONG JOKES


One day Leif Ericson came across a little lemming who was about to jump =
off a cliff into a river. Leif said, "Don't jump little lemming," and he =
gave the lemming to his assistant who taught it how to wade across the =
river instead of jumping off a cliff. The moral to this story is: If =
Leif hands you a lemming, make lemmings wade.  (Mother Goose & Grimm: =
Mike Peters) =20

My kids love going on the Web, and they keep track of their passwords =
(inappropriately, I might add) by writing them on Post-it notes. I =
noticed their Disney.com password was: =
"MickeyMinnieDonaldGoofyPlutoTiggerPoohStitch." I asked why it was so =
long. "Because," my son explained, "they said it had to have at least 8 =
characters."


